\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I bring my sins to Thee,
\par The sins I cannot count,
\par That all may cleansed be
\par In Thy once-opened Fount.
\par I bring them, Saviour, all to Thee;
\par The burden is too great for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. My heart to Thee I bring,
\par The heart I cannot read;
\par A faithless, wandering thing,
\par An evil heart indeed.
\par I bring it, saviour, now to Thee,
\par That fixed and faithful it may be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To thee I bring my care,
\par The care I cannot flee;
\par Thou will not only share,
\par But bear it all for me.
\par O loving Saviour, now to Thee
\par I bring the load that wearies me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I bring my grief to thee,
\par The grief I cannot tell;
\par No words shall needed be,
\par Thou knowest all so well.
\par I bring the sorrow laid on me,
\par O suffering Saviour, now to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. My joys to Thee I bring,
\par The joys Thy love hath given,
\par That each may be a wing
\par To lift me nearer heaven.
\par I bring them, Saviour, all to Thee;
\par For Thou hast purchased all for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. My life I bring to Thee,
\par I would not be my own;
\par O Saviour, let me be
\par Thine ever, Thine alone,
\par My heart, my life, my all I bring
\par To Thee, my Saviour and my King.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

